# family-hub/deploy/env.template — environment for the family-facing portal.
#
# On the droplet:   cp deploy/env.template /var/www/family-hub/.env
#                   chmod 600 /var/www/family-hub/.env
#
# Since v1.1.0 this file DOES hold one secret (FAMILY_SSO_SECRET), so chmod 600
# is no longer merely tidy. It still holds no ADMIN_KEY and no trip data: the
# portal is a launcher plus one shared sign-in, nothing else.
#
# HAZARD: the portal's home is /var/www/family-hub — NEVER under /var/www/trips,
# or it would discover itself as an "instance" and backup-all.sh would sweep it.
# (Same hazard as admin-hub; see docs/MULTI_INSTANCE.md §ADMIN-HUB.)
#
# PORT              — the portal's localhost port (nginx proxy_pass target for the apex domain).
# TRIPS_DIR         — where the trip instances live; each subdir with a .env is one instance.
# PUBLIC_SUFFIX     — trip URLs are built as https://<instance-name>.<PUBLIC_SUFFIX>
# FAMILY_NAMES      — comma-separated; who may sign in at the portal. Spelling must match
#                     the names in each trip's family list, or SSO lands on that trip's PIN
#                     screen instead (the trip only honors a cookie naming one of its own).
# FAMILY_SSO_SECRET — the ONE secret shared with every trip instance; it signs the fam_sso
#                     cookie each instance verifies. Generate + distribute with
#                     deploy/sync-sso-secret.sh (openssl rand -hex 24). LEAVE IT EMPTY to
#                     disable SSO: the portal keeps working as the Phase-1 launcher and no
#                     cookie is ever issued.
# COOKIE_DOMAIN     — the dot-prefixed parent domain the cookie is scoped to, e.g.
#                     .example.com, so every <trip>.example.com sees it. Leave EMPTY for
#                     localhost development (host-only cookie).
# PIN_PEPPER        — optional. Keys the portal's PIN hash (HMAC-SHA256) so a leaked users
#                     table isn't a 10,000-entry rainbow table away from every 4-digit PIN.
#                     EMPTY = the original bare-sha256 scheme, unchanged. Set it and each
#                     person migrates silently on their next sign-in — no reset needed.
#                     Never change or clear it once set: PINs hashed under the old value
#                     stop matching and must be reset. Independent of the trip instances'
#                     PIN_PEPPER — the portal has its own users table, so the values need
#                     not match (and there is no benefit to sharing one).
# FAMILY_ROSTER_LOCKED — optional. '1' = only names that already have a PIN may sign in,
#                     so nobody can claim a family member's name before they do. Leave EMPTY
#                     (the default) until everyone has set their PIN, then set it to 1 and
#                     reload. Admin PIN reset still re-opens a single name.
# NODE_ENV          — leave as production on the droplet.
PORT=3011
TRIPS_DIR=/var/www/trips
PUBLIC_SUFFIX=example.com
FAMILY_NAMES=Alex,Sam,Jordan,Riley,Casey
FAMILY_SSO_SECRET=
COOKIE_DOMAIN=.example.com
PIN_PEPPER=
FAMILY_ROSTER_LOCKED=
NODE_ENV=production
